From 5fd59833c70b930131b0de977c4ca08ccd44f718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:41:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] skill index: show triggers: frontmatter on index rows
 (skills.index_triggers, default on) [daveey]

A skill's triggers: mapping ({asks: [up to 3 user phrasings], not_for: str}) is appended to its
<available_skills> row as ' Asks: "a"; "b"; "c". Not for: x.'. extract_skill_description() stays
the one place rows are built (with_triggers=None reads config). The setting is part of the
in-process cache key and recorded in the disk snapshot (v6), so toggling it or editing triggers:
refreshes the index; v5 snapshots are rebuilt. Documented in creating-skills.md.

Measured with hermes-mods tools/skill-trigger-eval: weakest-30 recall 0.670 -> 0.829 (a description
rewrite alone 0.731); full index mean 0.921 -> 0.947, ~72 tokens per skill with triggers.
